   "stem": {
      "text": "Find the value of \\( \\lim_{\\Delta x \\to 0} \\frac{(5 + \\Delta x)^{2} - 25}{\\Delta x} \\)."
   },
   "answer_key": {
      "form": "symbolic",
      "mathjson": 10
   },
   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "The numerator has the form \\( f(5 + \\Delta x) - f(5) \\) with \\( f(x) = x^{2} \\), because \\( f(5) = 25 \\).",
         "mathjson": 25
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "So the function is \\( f(x) = x^{2} \\) and the base point is \\( x = 5 \\).",
         "mathjson": 5
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "The limit is the definition of \\( f'(5) \\), and \\( f'(x) = 2 x \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Multiply",
            2,
            "x"
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 4,
         "text": "Evaluate: \\( f'(5) = 10 \\).",
         "mathjson": 10
      }
